    {
      "skill_id": "fr-a1-021",
      "title": "Short past events: the passé composé",
      "explanation": "The passé composé describes a finished event. It has two parts: avoir or être in the present, then a past participle. Regular -er verbs form the participle by changing -er to -é: parler, parlé; manger, mangé. Frequent irregular participles: faire, fait; prendre, pris; avoir, eu; être, été. Most verbs use avoir: J'ai mangé. A few frequent verbs of movement, such as aller, arriver and rester, use être, and then the participle agrees with the subject: Il est arrivé, Elle est arrivée, Ils sont arrivés. A time word such as hier (yesterday) often goes with it.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "fr": "J'ai chanté hier.",
          "en": "I sang yesterday."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Elle est arrivée hier.",
          "en": "She arrived yesterday."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Nous avons fait les courses.",
          "en": "We did the shopping."
        }
      ],
      "references": ["FEI-INV"],
