      "skill_id": "fr-a1-022",
      "title": "Something just happened: venir de + infinitive",
      "explanation": "To say that something has just happened, use the present of venir, then de, then an infinitive: Je viens de manger. De becomes d' before a vowel or a silent h: Elle vient d'arriver. Venir is irregular: je viens, tu viens, il/elle/on vient, nous venons, vous venez, ils/elles viennent. The infinitive never changes.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "fr": "Je viens de travailler.",
          "en": "I have just worked."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Marie vient d'arriver.",
          "en": "Marie has just arrived."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Ils viennent de chanter.",
          "en": "They have just sung."
        }
