    {
      "skill_id": "fr-a1-024",
      "title": "There is and there are: il y a",
      "explanation": "Il y a means there is or there are, and it does not change for singular or plural: Il y a un livre sur la table, Il y a des fleurs dans le jardin. It is followed by an article and a noun, often with a place. To ask, use intonation or est-ce que: Est-ce qu'il y a un restaurant ici ? After a negative the article becomes de or d': Il n'y a pas de lait. Do not use il est for this meaning.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "fr": "Il y a un livre dans le sac.",
          "en": "There is a book in the bag."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Il y a des fleurs dans le jardin.",
          "en": "There are flowers in the garden."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Il n'y a pas de lait.",
          "en": "There is no milk."
        }
